      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1735750508667,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Parses kernel binary sections and physical memory addresses:\n\n    1. Physical addresses help determine the available RAM.\n    2. Kernel sections indicate the kernel's location, preventing memory reuse.\n    3. The Multiboot 2 info address shows its location to avoid overwriting.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "F4nJPrJUIsepPa0VV5b-5",
      "originalText": "Parses kernel binary sections and physical memory addresses:\n\n    1. Physical addresses help determine the available RAM.\n    2. Kernel sections indicate the kernel's location, preventing memory reuse.\n    3. The Multiboot 2 info address shows its location to avoid overwriting.",
