    {
      "id": "_gKG-vDwgW_HXd7tkytVr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -92.22695808071467,
      "y": 1560.6186782588893,
      "width": 738.1,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "bqS1MliFArX1Qe1Lp6Es8"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1182661121,
      "version": 298,
      "versionNonce": 1953092903,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "E-u77MN0VfXhKBXYGGn_o",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1735750508667,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nA simple memory allocator that sequentially increments a pointer to allocate\nphysical frames, mapping physical memory into 4 KiB chunks. It uses the\naddresses of the kernel and Multiboot 2 info to ensure reserved regions\nare not allocated. This approach is fast and efficient for linear allocation\npatterns but does not support deallocation or reuse of memory.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nA simple memory allocator that sequentially increments a pointer to allocate\nphysical frames, mapping physical memory into 4 KiB chunks. It uses the\naddresses of the kernel and Multiboot 2 info to ensure reserved regions\nare not allocated. This approach is fast and efficient for linear allocation\npatterns but does not support deallocation or reuse of memory.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
